YAML features found (grep for `&`, `*`, `!` at the start of a value and
for `---`):
- No anchor (`&`), alias (`*`) or tag (`!`) starts a value in either file.
- Both files begin with a `---` document marker on line 1 (a single
  document; there is no second `---`). The locale reader must accept one
  leading `---`.
- Block sequences are written at their parent key's indentation
  (`abbr_day_names:` then `    - Sun` at the same column as the key).
- A sequence item can be empty: `-` alone in en.yml, `- ` (with a
  trailing space) in ja.yml (month_names[0] and abbr_month_names[0]).
- ja.yml's `date.order` items are `:year`, `:month`, `:day`, which
  CRuby's YAML.safe_load refuses (Psych::DisallowedClass: Symbol); the
  locale reader keeps them as the text ":year".
- Unquoted YAML 1.1 scalars that Psych would type: `precision: 3`,
  `significant: false` (kept as the text "3", "false"; plan decision D4).
- No block scalar (`|`, `>`), no flow collection, no `\u` escape.
